AutofillManager: Do not call the service when the device has no autofill

The Echos leave out android.software.autofill, so SystemServer never
starts AutofillManagerService and mService is null. Most entry points
return early through hasAutofillFeature(), but some did not. A filled-in,
unfocused EditText that became visible went through
notifyViewVisibilityChanged() to ensureServiceClientAddedIfNeededLocked(),
which called mService.addClient() and crashed the app with a
NullPointerException (issue #24).

Return early there and in the other public methods that called mService
without the check. Without a client mEnabled stays false, so no session
starts and nothing else reaches mService.

